    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The discount, in plain numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>$150 a month instead of $175 a month.</strong> Nothing down at signing, and the discount applies for the entire duration of the engagement rather than just the first year. That works out to $300 saved every year you stay.</li>
      <li><strong>Same plan, same scope, same everything.</strong> The discounted rate covers the full standard plan, including the design, the custom-coded build, the hosting, the unlimited content updates, the blog system, and direct support from me.</li>
      <li><strong>Free 5-point audit either way.</strong> If you are not yet ready to build, the <a href="/audit/" class="inline-link">free audit</a> is also free, and I will flag you for the discount the day you do hire me.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who qualifies</h2>
    <p>Any licensed medical, dental, allied-health, or mental-health professional in active practice or licensed retirement, plus their immediate family:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Physicians.</strong> MDs, DOs, residents, fellows.</li>
      <li><strong>Dental.</strong> DDS / DMD, dental hygienists, oral surgeons, orthodontists, endodontists, periodontists, prosthodontists.</li>
      <li><strong>Nursing.</strong> RNs, LPNs / LVNs, NPs, CRNAs, midwives, nursing assistants.</li>
      <li><strong>Allied health.</strong> PAs, physical therapists, occupational therapists, speech-language pathologists, audiologists, respiratory therapists, optometrists, opticians, podiatrists, chiropractors, registered dietitians, pharmacists.</li>
      <li><strong>Mental health.</strong> Licensed psychologists, LCSWs / LMFTs / LPCs / LMHCs, board-certified psychiatrists, board-certified behavior analysts.</li>
      <li><strong>Medical imaging and lab.</strong> Radiologic technologists, sonographers, medical lab scientists, phlebotomists with state licensure.</li>
      <li><strong>Spouses, children, parents, and siblings</strong> of any qualifying clinician, same discount, same verification (one shared photo of the clinician's license, plus a one-line note identifying the relationship).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>How verification works:</strong> One photo or scan of your active license, state board card, hospital ID with clinical role visible, or a current verification printout from your state licensing board. Email it once when we start; I delete the file the moment I confirm. I do not retain copies of your documents.</p>

    <h2>How to claim it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Book a 20-minute discovery call.</strong> <a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Standard contact form</a>. In the message, mention you are claiming the medical personnel discount.</li>
      <li><strong>On the call, we figure out the build.</strong> Same conversation I have with anyone, what your practice needs, which plan fits, which features matter. (If you are HIPAA-touching with intake forms, I will walk you through the appropriate intake-form provider; I do not handle PHI directly.)</li>
      <li><strong>Send proof of license.</strong> One photo of your license card or a current state-board verification, by email. Takes 30 seconds.</li>
      <li><strong>I apply the discount on day one.</strong> Your first invoice is at the discounted rate, not the standard rate. There is no "ramp" or "after first year" reset.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>A note on HIPAA and intake forms</h2>
    <p>I build the marketing site itself, namely the pages, the blog, the service descriptions, the hours, and the location. <strong>I do not store or process PHI on the website.</strong> Patient intake, scheduling, and any form that collects personal health information goes through a HIPAA-compliant third-party provider, such as Jotform HIPAA, Tebra, SimplePractice, or Healee, depending on your specialty. Your site links to and embeds those forms, but the data does not pass through my servers. We will set this up correctly together during the build.</p>

    <h2>Why I do this</h2>
    <p>A meaningful number of clinicians are launching independent or part-time private practice as the healthcare landscape continues to shift. The licensing and credentialing burden is enormous, the schedule is brutal, and the work has real human stakes attached to it. If a $25-a-month gap is the difference between having a real website and not, that is a gap worth closing.</p>

